{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on G's repair loop, after the third END with exit 1 (f05f3886).\n\nThree sealed runs stopped at compiler-06, the CLI's tsconfig.scope.json,\nand no test ran in any of them. A sealed packet is the wrong tool for a\ntype error.\n\n1. Before the next continuation, run compiler-06 by itself on the repair\n   until it exits 0. Then run each other compiler context that reads the\n   files of the repair. These are working checks. They need no packet,\n   no freezer, no seal and no audit, and they are not acceptance\n   evidence. The local slot is free for them.\n2. Start one sealed continuation when those checks pass. Its packet is\n   the evidence.\n3. The three failed units stay as they are.\n4. AGENTS.md says to run the tests of what you change while you work,\n   and the gate once before review. A compiler run of one config is such\n   a test.\n\nThe hold on main at 9f3338ff stands until G lands.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}